        "DO NOT LAUNCH": 0.0
      }
    },
    "finding": "On RAW the estimator is UNBIASED (bias -0.031 pp) and the 95% CI covers the true value 94% of the time (nominal 95%). WINSORIZATION introduces a small NEGATIVE bias (-0.36 pp) because it clips the treatment's high values more (multiplicative effect) -> coverage drops to 92%. That is the price of the variance reduction. The +5.7% of the SEED=42 split falls within the p2.5-p97.5 range.",
    "decision_rule_power_finding": "The power to REJECT H0 (100%) is NOT the power of the full decision rule. With the winsorized cap, the gate '95% CI entirely > +3%' -> LAUNCH fires in 50% of the 500 re-randomizations (ITERATE 50%, DO NOT LAUNCH 0%). The SEED=42 split (which did give LAUNCH) benefited from a favorable baseline imbalance -- it is not representative of the other half of re-randomizations. 'The design is amply powered' is true for H0, not for the business decision actually made."
  },
